{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And on the eighth day.</b> Our Sages of blessed memory said: 'on the day' and not at night. Now, one born half an hour before sunset will be circumcised after six and a half days, for a Torah day is not from time to time." "<b>ימול.</b> From the nifal paradigm, like לא יכון, and it is from the root מולים היו [they were circumcised]. It is also possible that it is lacking a nun, from the root ונמלתם, like איש כי ידור נדר, and the mem is absent, like אביו or בית דין." "<b>ערלתו.</b> Known, for it is in the [context of] nakedness, unlike 'foreskin of heart' and 'lip' and 'ear,' for all of them are construct forms."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "Reading 'וחסר המל' as 'וחסר המ״ם' (the letter mem), based on context; the manuscripts may vary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:43.236139007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}